---
import ModernLayout from '../../../layouts/ModernLayout.astro';
---
<ModernLayout
  title="Open Dental Readiness | Donovan Family Dentistry"
  description="A private, noindex implementation checklist for connecting verified Open Dental patient tools to the Donovan Family Dentistry website."
  forceNoIndex={true}
>
  <section class="modern-page-hero">
    <div class="modern-shell modern-page-hero__grid">
      <div>
        <p class="modern-kicker">Private office readiness</p>
        <h1>Use Open Dental first—without duplicating the practice system.</h1>
      </div>
      <p class="modern-page-hero__aside">This page is an office checklist, not a patient portal. It stores nothing, requests no credentials, and must never contain patient information or API keys.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="modern-section modern-section--sand">
    <div class="modern-shell modern-visit-grid">
      <article class="modern-visit-card">
        <p class="modern-eyebrow">Recommended first</p>
        <h2>Connect tools already available through Open Dental.</h2>
        <ol class="modern-checklist">
          <li><strong>Web Forms:</strong> confirm the office is on active support, build or approve the registration and medical-history Sheets, enable the mobile layout, and obtain the exact patient link.</li>
          <li><strong>Patient Portal:</strong> decide which portal features the office will expose and obtain the office-specific portal link.</li>
          <li><strong>eReminders and General Messages:</strong> inventory what is already enabled before purchasing another communication platform.</li>
          <li><strong>Web Sched:</strong> consider online scheduling only after appointment types, providers, operatories, availability rules, and staff ownership are approved.</li>
        </ol>
      </article>

      <aside class="modern-visit-card" aria-labelledby="open-dental-order-heading">
        <p class="modern-eyebrow">Why this order</p>
        <h3 id="open-dental-order-heading">Avoid paying twice.</h3>
        <p>Open Dental already holds the practice records. Linking its approved patient tools directly can reduce duplicate forms, double entry, competing reminders, and conflicting appointment workflows.</p>
        <p><a href="https://www.opendental.com/site/eservices.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Review Open Dental eServices</a></p>
        <p><a href="https://www.opendental.com/site/fees.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Review current Open Dental fees</a></p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="modern-section modern-section--deep">
    <div class="modern-shell modern-visit-grid">
      <article>
        <p class="modern-eyebrow">Website integration rules</p>
        <h2>Link to the approved workflow; do not recreate it here.</h2>
        <ul class="modern-bring-list">
          <li>Use only exact HTTPS links copied from the office's Open Dental setup.</li>
          <li>Open Web Forms as a direct page rather than placing them inside an iframe.</li>
          <li>Keep patient data, API keys, registration keys, credentials, and completed forms out of this public repository.</li>
          <li>Do not send medical, dental, insurance, payment, or appointment details through the general administrative inquiry form.</li>
          <li>Use the Open Dental API—not direct database writes—if the practice later approves a custom two-way integration.</li>
          <li>Require an appropriate agreement, least-privilege access, audit review, downtime procedures, and office testing before enabling any PHI-capable integration.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <aside class="modern-visit-card" aria-labelledby="open-dental-activation-heading">
        <h3 id="open-dental-activation-heading">Office activation checklist</h3>
        <ol class="modern-checklist">
          <li>Confirm the Open Dental version, support status, eConnector health, and enabled eServices.</li>
          <li>Choose the first patient feature to activate; Web Forms is the recommended starting point.</li>
          <li>Copy the exact office-specific URL without entering credentials into GitHub or Pages CMS.</li>
          <li>Test the complete workflow with office-approved non-production test data.</li>
          <li>Verify import, matching, staff notifications, failure handling, and correction procedures.</li>
          <li>Only then add the verified link to Patient Forms or New Patients.</li>
        </ol>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="modern-section">
    <div class="modern-shell modern-visit-grid">
      <article class="modern-visit-card">
        <p class="modern-eyebrow">Official references</p>
        <h2>Use Open Dental's current documentation during setup.</h2>
        <ul class="modern-policy-list">
          <li><a href="https://www.opendental.com/site/webforms.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Web Forms feature</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.opendental.com/site/patientportal.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Patient Portal feature</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.opendental.com/site/websched.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Web Sched feature</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.opendental.com/manual/eservicessetup.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">eServices setup</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.opendental.com/manual/fhir.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">API setup and third-party access</a></li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <aside class="modern-visit-card" aria-labelledby="open-dental-state-heading">
        <p class="modern-eyebrow">Current website state</p>
        <h3 id="open-dental-state-heading">No patient-system link is active yet.</h3>
        <p>The website continues to provide downloadable blank PDFs and a non-PHI administrative contact path. Open Dental links remain intentionally absent until the office supplies and tests its exact URLs.</p>
        <a class="modern-button modern-button--secondary" href="/review/">Return to device review</a>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</ModernLayout>
